":false,"_score_incr_roic":33.1,"_gate_margin_advantage":-12.012152078819462,"_gp_margin_advantage":false,"_score_margin_advantage":0.0,"_gate_pool_share":null,"_gp_pool_share":null,"_score_pool_share":null,"_gate_rev_durability":null,"_gp_rev_durability":null,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":-0.1707405577271521,"_gp_margins":false,"_score_margins":0.0,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.0,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":11.1,"_gate_share_shrink":0.7983292875091459,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":2.48377539503386,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.01692,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":11.3,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Rigetti Computing, Inc., through its subsidiaries, builds and operates quantum computers and the superconducting quantum processors the United States, the United Kingdom, rest of Europe, Asia, and internationally. The company offers quantum processing units (QPUs) and quantum computing systems to provide access to quantum computing systems through the cloud in the form of quantum computing as a service (QCaaS). It provides Novera, a 9-qubit chip QPU that features tunable couplers for fast two-qubit operations and a 5-qubit chip for testing single-qubit operations; Novera QPU that is based in fourth generation Ankaa-class architecture; 36-qubit Cepheus-1-36Q system, a multi-chip quantum computer; and 84-qubit Ankaa-3 quantum computer. The company also sells access to its quantum computers through QCaaS. In addition, the company offers Rigetti quantum cloud services, a platform that provides support for various range of programming capabilities, public or private clouds integration, and connectivity, as well as quantum operating system software that supports public and private cloud architectures. Further, it offers QCS Outpost, a distributed software environment for operating, administering, and monitoring the overall system; Rigetti Foundry Services that delivers superconducting quantum chips to advance and accelerate quantum information science and technology research and development; and professional services, such as algorithm development, benchmarking, quantum application programming, and software development. The company serves commercial enterprises, government organizations, and international government entities, as well as academia, defense laboratories, and national laboratories. Rigetti Computing, Inc. was founded in 2013 and is headquartered in Berkeley, California.","ceo_bio":"Dr. Subodh K. Kulkarni Ph.D. | CEO, President & Director | Age 60 | Compensation: $636,222 (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 162 people. Revenue per employee of $44K ranks in the bottom quartile among Technology peers, with revenue falling 19%/yr across its filed history. Stock-based compensation of $109K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 15\u00d7 revenue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (9/10).","financial_summary":["Rigetti Computing, Inc. is a mid-cap technology business with a $3.3B market cap on $7M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -19% over the past three years, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at -370% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests. Gross margins of 65% confirm genuine pricing power.","The company is burning through $77M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, interest coverage of 40\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and stock-based comp at 248% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (20.0% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom decile among Technology peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of","sev":"red","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Revenue growth in the bottom decile of Technology peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"red","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Operating margins 1201% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $20.1M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 62/100): structural revenue/margin decline; roic below cost of capital \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Technology peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Cybersecurity liability and talent cost inflation \u2014 a single breach can erase years of goodwill, and the war for engineering talent compresses margins even at scale.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Valued at a 292% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA",